# emu-sources — the uxncli translation units, in ONE place.
#
# Sourced (`. ./emu-sources`) by build.sh (host) and cross-build.sh (armhf/arm64). The
# compile line used to exist twice — build.sh's host build and verify-note3.sh's inline
# armhf cross-build — and a third copy for arm64 is exactly the drift the genome keeps
# finding: one copy gains a device, the others quietly do not, and the platforms disagree
# about what the emulator IS.
#
# net.c is load-bearing. Dropping it from this list fails LOUD at link (uxncli.c references
# net_dei/net_deo unconditionally), so THIS list cannot silently lose the device. The silent
# failure is a net-BLIND stub build, where emu_dei falls through to `return uxn.dev[addr]`
# = 0 and net state 0 is Disconnected — a ROM then answers `NA` rc=2, byte-identical on
# stdout to a genuine connection refused. That is why cross-build.sh --check IDENTIFIES the
# device (action d0) instead of trusting that this file was right.
EMU_SRC="src/uxncli.c src/uxn.c src/devices/system.c src/devices/console.c src/devices/file.c src/devices/datetime.c src/devices/net.c"
